  "externalCurriculum": {
    "year1": "10 compulsory 6 EC units. Appendix 1 p. 21 and the Study Guide agree on identities, credits and periods.",
    "year2": "24 EC required track units, 12 EC required PPE in Practice, 24 EC restricted electives. Ethics II and International Trade are P4, History of Philosophy II and Global Justice P5. Three philosophy and one economics electives meet Article 11.4’s at-least-one-per-track rule and the annual plan’s two-per-period placement.",
    "year3": "30 EC approved study abroad in P1–3, 6 EC qualitative methods and 6 EC tutorial in P4, 12 EC thesis in P5 and 6 EC PPE in Practice V in P6. The methods/policy alternative and internship/minor routes are excluded from this illustration.",
    "progression": "OER 9.1 and thesis guide state 108 Year-1/2 EC by end of P3, with a 102 EC conditional route. Tutorial guide also prints 138 total EC and a separate 108 EC provisional threshold. The illustrated 120 Year-1/2 plus 30 study-abroad EC before P4 satisfies both ordinary thresholds. Thesis intent is registered in September. OER attendance and BSA conditions are non-credit. The thesis may use one or more PPE disciplines.",
    "identity": "English, full-time, 180 EC VU bachelor, RIO 54999, September 2026 basis. Appendix 1 orders Philosophy and Economics first among equal-depth pairings. The route was selected independently of UCR availability."
  },
